01:07:01,686 --> 01:07:02,812
I won't stay!

1049
01:07:04,355 --> 01:07:06,232
This just isn't doing anything
for me anymore.

1050
01:07:06,983 --> 01:07:08,109
What do you mean?

1051
01:07:09,318 --> 01:07:11,988
It's not getting me off
or turning me on at all.

1052
01:07:12,154 --> 01:07:14,615
Well, do you want
to torture him or something?

1053
01:07:14,740 --> 01:07:16,742
Don't! Please, help me!

1054
01:07:16,867 --> 01:07:19,287
Are we supposed to just keep
doing this forever ?

1055
01:07:19,412 --> 01:07:21,163
I don't know.
Yeah.

1056
01:07:22,123 --> 01:07:24,750
Let's just get this over with.
It's gonna be dawn.

1057
01:07:47,398 --> 01:07:49,233
Hurry. Hurry.

1058
01:07:52,737 --> 01:07:53,738
What?

1059
01:07:54,864 --> 01:07:57,116
We haven't almost gotten caught
in the dawn in over a century.

1060
01:08:00,161 --> 01:08:01,704
Joan, what are you doing?
Get in here.

1061
01:08:03,539 --> 01:08:04,415
Joan.

1062
01:08:06,542 --> 01:08:08,336
I don't feel anything anymore.

1063
01:08:09,378 --> 01:08:10,212
What?

1064
01:08:12,548 --> 01:08:13,966
I want to see the sunrise.

1065
01:08:16,385 --> 01:08:17,303
Come with me.

1066
01:08:18,179 --> 01:08:19,597
You said we could sleep
in the same coffin together.

1067
01:08:19,722 --> 01:08:21,265
You're being crazy.

1068
01:08:21,390 --> 01:08:22,933
- Get in here now.
- I'm not crazy.

1069
01:08:24,060 --> 01:08:25,311
- Elizabeth--
- Get in here.

1070
01:08:26,062 --> 01:08:27,605
- Come with me, please.
- Joan.

1071
01:08:27,730 --> 01:08:29,482
- Please. It'll be so beautiful.
- No--

1072
01:08:29,607 --> 01:08:31,400
Come on.

1073
01:08:32,234 --> 01:08:34,362
Don't do this, Joan.
Don't leave me.

1074
01:08:34,487 --> 01:08:35,446
- Please.
- Joan.

1075
01:08:35,571 --> 01:08:38,199
- I'm sorry. I have to.
- No. No.

1076
01:08:38,532 --> 01:08:40,910
Joan! Joan! Joan!

1077
01:08:43,204 --> 01:08:44,622
Oh, my God.

1078
01:09:11,315 --> 01:09:12,400
I'll go somewhere.

1079
01:09:13,651 --> 01:09:14,902
It's so beautiful.

1080
01:09:41,721 --> 01:09:43,222
We put the devil to sleep.

1081
01:09:45,057 --> 01:09:46,016
Where is Joan?

1082
01:09:48,644 --> 01:09:50,521
The sky is red as fire by now.

1083
01:09:52,273 --> 01:09:54,567
Joan went crazy
and destroyed herself.

1084
01:09:54,817 --> 01:09:55,818
What?

1085
01:09:56,736 --> 01:09:59,613
We made it back to the bar
just as the sun was coming up,

1086
01:09:59,739 --> 01:10:06,537
and Joan just turned around
and ran off into the daylight.

1087
01:10:22,261 --> 01:10:23,429
I'm not feeling well.

1088
01:10:23,804 --> 01:10:24,680
I'm hungry.

1089
01:10:26,140 --> 01:10:28,100
Let's make a steak
and drink some ice water.

1090
01:10:28,934 --> 01:10:29,977
It's going to be a long night.

1091
01:10:30,102 --> 01:10:32,104
Albert's not getting here
until tomorrow morning.

1092
01:10:39,278 --> 01:10:40,613
Are you scared of me?

1093
01:10:42,448 --> 01:10:43,574
I feel fucked up.

1094
01:10:44,492 --> 01:10:46,786
I need to get a bottle of vodka
to get through this,

1095
01:10:47,536 --> 01:10:48,996
then we can have steak.

1096
01:10:57,338 --> 01:10:58,756
We're not supposed
to go out tonight.

1097
01:10:59,507 --> 01:11:00,549
It's the eclipse.

1098
01:11:01,008 --> 01:11:02,468
I'll be back in five minutes.

1099
01:11:05,721 --> 01:11:06,847
The mischief.

1100
01:11:52,184 --> 01:11:53,936
Oh, I do feel it.

1101
01:11:58,357 --> 01:11:59,650
I'm a devil tonight.

1102
01:12:01,443 --> 01:12:03,070
Oh, yeah.

1103
01:12:03,654 --> 01:12:06,699
Ramsey the Devil,
it's a perfect night

1104
01:12:07,366 --> 01:12:09,827
every night
with Ramsey the Devil.

1105
01:12:11,453 --> 01:12:12,371
Let's do this.

1106
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:20,421
I'm Ramsey the Devil tonight
and every night.

1107
01:12:20,838 --> 01:12:22,423
Whooh! Yeah!

1108
01:12:23,382 --> 01:12:24,341
Weow!

1109
01:12:42,651 --> 01:12:45,279
Stupid glitching
smart technology.

1110
01:12:45,696 --> 01:12:48,324
My phone really wants me
to talk to this guy Ramsey.

1111
01:13:03,756 --> 01:13:05,049
This is a weird glitch.

1112
01:13:05,257 --> 01:13:06,133
Hey there.

1113
01:13:06,258 --> 01:13:07,509
You didn't cause it,
did you?

1114
01:13:07,760 --> 01:13:08,928
No, I didn't.

1115
01:13:09,386 --> 01:13:12,473
Aren't these apps just designed
to connect people anyway?

1116
01:13:13,015 --> 01:13:16,101
Yeah. I suppose they are.

1117
01:13:16,936 --> 01:13:18,062
Maybe it's a sign.

1118
01:13:18,979 --> 01:13:22,316
Or maybe the smart technology
wanted us to meet up.

1119
01:13:23,400 --> 01:13:24,735
Okay, I'm bored enough
to meet you.

1120
01:13:24,860 --> 01:13:26,445
I've been in my apartment
for days.

1121
01:13:26,570 --> 01:13:29,365
What about that restaurant
Annabelle's downtown?

1122
01:13:29,490 --> 01:13:30,407
They're open late.

1123
01:13:30,950 --> 01:13:33,243
Oh, of course.
I love that place.

1124
01:13:33,410 --> 01:13:35,371
You want to meet me there
in a half hour?

1125
01:13:35,788 --> 01:13:37,164
Perfect.
Can you order for me?

1126
01:13:37,289 --> 01:13:38,958
I think I might be
a couple minutes late.

1127
01:13:39,291 --> 01:13:41,752
Of course I can.
I'll see you soon.

1128
01:14:48,318 --> 01:14:49,987
- Hey.
- Hi, Ramsey.

1129
01:14:50,112 --> 01:14:51,655
- Yes. How are you?
- Hey.

1130
01:14:51,780 --> 01:14:52,781
Please, please.

1131
01:14:56,118 --> 01:14:57,161
Well, this is...

1132
01:14:57,828 --> 01:14:59,455
nice and unexpected.

1133
01:14:59,580 --> 01:15:00,539
I know, right?

1134
01:15:01,040 --> 01:15:03,167
Yeah, I wasn't even gonna
come out tonight either,

1135
01:15:03,292 --> 01:15:05,210
but I'm glad I did.

1136
01:15:06,420 --> 01:15:07,963
You look even nicer in person.

1137
01:15:08,672 --> 01:15:09,506
Thank you.

1138
01:15:11,759 --> 01:15:15,304
So pizza and absinthe,
those are brave choices.

1139
01:15:16,138 --> 01:15:17,306
It's a brave new world.

1140
01:15:18,891 --> 01:15:20,559
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1141
01:15:26,065 --> 01:15:27,941
You have such a pretty smile.

1142
01:15:28,192 --> 01:15:30,235
Oh. Thank you.
So do you.

1143
01:15:31,695 --> 01:15:33,197
I didn't know they
had absinthe here.

1144
01:15:34,948 --> 01:15:36,158
I know, odd, right?
Yeah.

1145
01:15:36,283 --> 01:15:37,618
They-- they do.

1146
01:15:37,743 --> 01:15:38,660
It's funny.

1147
01:15:49,379 --> 01:15:50,255
Come on right up.

1148
01:15:50,380 --> 01:15:51,298
- Whoa.
- Goddamnit!

1149
01:15:51,423 --> 01:15:53,008
- Come on, you wanna go? Come on.
- You wanna...

1150
01:15:53,300 --> 01:15:54,218
Shit!

1151
01:16:02,351 --> 01:16:03,185
- Whoa.
- Fuck you.

1152
01:16:03,310 --> 01:16:04,436
Everyone's going berserk.

1153
01:16:14,113 --> 01:16:14,988
Let's get out of here.

1154
01:17:21,471 --> 01:17:22,556
{\an8}Alexis?

1155
01:17:35,944 --> 01:17:36,862
Fuck.

1156
01:17:45,329 --> 01:17:47,080
I've never seen anything
like that before.

1157
01:17:47,497 --> 01:17:48,916
No, that was pretty extreme.

1158
01:17:50,000 --> 01:17:51,668
Yeah, that wasn't
just a bar fight.

1159
01:17:52,002 --> 01:17:53,921
It erupted too quickly
and with too much energy,

1160
01:17:54,046 --> 01:17:55,464
and people were stabbing
each other in the throats

1161
01:17:55,589 --> 01:17:56,506
with forks.

1162
01:17:56,632 --> 01:17:57,841
Yeah, it
wasn't just a bar fight.

1163
01:17:57,966 --> 01:17:58,926
Nah, you're right.

1164
01:17:59,968 --> 01:18:01,053
Doesn't make any sense.

1165
01:18:01,470 --> 01:18:02,930
I mean, I walked out
holding my drink.

1166
01:18:03,305 --> 01:18:05,390
Well, you were probably
just in shock.

1167
01:18:05,974 --> 01:18:06,850
Sure.

1168
01:18:08,060 --> 01:18:09,519
Hey, come check this out.

1169
01:18:10,187 --> 01:18:11,230
It's pretty cool in here.

1170
01:18:13,273 --> 01:18:14,233
What a night, huh?

1171
01:18:14,358 --> 01:18:15,317
Mm-hmm.

1172
01:18:22,407 --> 01:18:23,283
Hm.

1173
01:18:23,825 --> 01:18:25,160
Sure is a beautiful night.

1174
01:18:27,246 --> 01:18:28,163
Look at that moon.

1175
01:18:33,794 --> 01:18:35,212
Ramsey, where are we going?

1176
01:18:36,630 --> 01:18:38,465
I just thought we needed
to calm down a bit

1177
01:18:38,590 --> 01:18:39,591
after all that.

1178
01:18:40,926 --> 01:18:43,387
This place is beautiful here.

1179
01:18:45,055 --> 01:18:47,057
What could be mellower
than here, right?

1180
01:18:47,849 --> 01:18:50,310
Why don't we call it a night?
Talk later.

1181
01:18:50,727 --> 01:18:51,895
I don't think so.

1182
01:18:52,813 --> 01:18:54,815
I'm Ramsay the Devil, baby.

1183
01:18:56,108 --> 01:18:59,444
Let's just get this awkward
first kiss over with, shall we?

1184
01:18:59,653 --> 01:19:00,654
Come on!

1185
01:19:04,992 --> 01:19:06,410
You can't hurt me!

1186
01:19:07,119 --> 01:19:11,415
This is your lucky night
with Ramsey the Devil, baby.

1187
01:19:11,957 --> 01:19:14,459
Every night's a lucky night
with me!

1188
01:19:26,346 --> 01:19:27,764
You suspicious weirdo.

1189
01:19:29,057 --> 01:19:31,184
I suspected you might
be a blood-sucking fiend,

1190
01:19:31,310 --> 01:19:33,145
and that was half
the reason I came out.

1191
01:19:33,687 --> 01:19:34,604
Oh, yeah?

1192
01:19:35,647 --> 01:19:36,815
What's the other half?

1193
01:19:37,733 --> 01:19:38,900
That doesn't matter now.

1194
01:19:39,901 --> 01:19:41,361
And I know they
don't serve absinthe

1195
01:19:41,486 --> 01:19:43,071
at that Italian restaurant.

1196
01:19:46,033 --> 01:19:46,867
Shut up.

1197
01:19:47,034 --> 01:19:48,243
I'm Ramsey the Devil.

1198
01:19:50,078 --> 01:19:51,747
I'm gonna eat you up,
little girl.

1199
01:19:58,086 --> 01:19:59,212
- Really?
- Yeah!

1200
01:20:28,492 --> 01:20:30,035
It's your lucky night, baby.

1201
01:20:30,660 --> 01:20:31,912
Oh yeah.

1202
01:20:46,259 --> 01:20:47,636
I'm Ramsey the Devil.

1203
01:20:50,055 --> 01:20:52,015
Oh, this shit is solid silver.

1204
01:20:53,475 --> 01:20:54,935
See, I know what I'm doing.

1205
01:20:55,727 --> 01:20:57,354
I'm gonna send you
back to hell.

1206
01:20:57,479 --> 01:20:58,772
I was never in hell.

1207
01:20:58,897 --> 01:21:00,148
Right were you belong?

1208
01:21:00,941 --> 01:21:01,775
Oh.

1209
01:21:01,983 --> 01:21:03,902
Well, I hope you like
inviting innocent girls out

1210
01:21:04,027 --> 01:21:05,112
to dinner in hell.

1211
01:21:05,445 --> 01:21:07,364
Because that's where you'll
be eating the rest

1212
01:21:07,489 --> 01:21:08,740
of your hot meals.

1213
01:21:13,537 --> 01:21:15,122
I guess that's it for you.

1214
01:21:16,164 --> 01:21:18,917
Dating is really
dangerous nowadays.

1215
01:21:20,168 --> 01:21:22,212
You never know
what you can get out there...

1216
01:21:23,171 --> 01:21:24,923
Ramsey the Devil.

1217
01:21:39,479 --> 01:21:40,564
I'm Ramsey the Devil.

1218
01:22:29,321 --> 01:22:32,657
Elizabeth!
That's you, isn't it?

1219
01:22:33,158 --> 01:22:35,285
Yes, it's me.

1220
01:22:36,745 --> 01:22:38,246
Why don't you come out
and fight?

1221
01:22:38,955 --> 01:22:40,373
Oh, it won't be a fight.

1222
01:22:40,916 --> 01:22:42,626
You destroyed my new friend,

1223
01:22:42,751 --> 01:22:44,836
and I'm getting tired
of losing friends.

1224
01:22:44,961 --> 01:22:46,213
That was your friend?

1225
01:22:48,381 --> 01:22:49,466
That guy sucked!

1226
01:23:02,646 --> 01:23:05,190
Stupid intelligence officer.

1227
01:23:08,235 --> 01:23:09,819
What are you doing?

1228
01:23:10,987 --> 01:23:13,240
You're not even supposed
to be out tonight.

1229
01:23:22,457 --> 01:23:23,875
Bye-bye, sugar pie.

1230
01:23:26,878 --> 01:23:27,921
Oh, come on.

1231
01:23:54,239 --> 01:23:56,157
I've wasted a lot of time.

1232
01:23:57,075 --> 01:23:58,535
Now you're going to die.

1233
01:23:58,660 --> 01:23:59,869
Get this thing off me.

1234
01:24:00,829 --> 01:24:01,663
Come on.

1235
01:24:05,875 --> 01:24:08,253
No. No, no, no.

1236
01:24:09,838 --> 01:24:10,839
You know you're lucky.

1237
01:24:11,423 --> 01:24:12,882
- Oh, yeah?
- Mm.

1238
01:24:13,216 --> 01:24:16,469
You're about to go to the
Kingdom of Paradise, right?

1239
01:24:17,262 --> 01:24:18,179
I don't want to.

1240
01:24:20,515 --> 01:24:24,394
While me...
I'll just linger here forever.

1241
01:24:25,061 --> 01:24:26,730
You could pray for redemption.

1242
01:24:27,939 --> 01:24:29,441
I could give you peace.

1243
01:24:31,693 --> 01:24:33,403
See the stairway to heaven.

1244
01:25:04,726 --> 01:25:05,894
There you are.

1245
01:25:48,687 --> 01:25:50,689
You can't resist me.

1246
01:25:51,523 --> 01:25:52,816
Embrace me.

1247
01:25:54,275 --> 01:25:56,027
I'm gonna mutilate you.

1248
01:26:00,740 --> 01:26:06,121
Alexis was dead,
and the long nights were back.

1249
01:26:08,164 --> 01:26:09,791
The old nights.

1250
01:26:11,209 --> 01:26:12,919
The broken nights,

1251
01:26:14,879 --> 01:26:17,590
the all-or-nothing nights,

1252
01:26:19,384 --> 01:26:22,762
the nights of blood and tears.

1253
01:26:26,057 --> 01:26:29,310
Don't think about me,
happy thoughts.

1254
01:26:33,231 --> 01:26:34,357
Happy thoughts.

1255
01:26:54,461 --> 01:26:55,420
What are we gonna do now?

1256
01:26:55,545 --> 01:26:59,299
Just open the bar
without Joan like normal?

1257
01:27:00,049 --> 01:27:01,634
Calm down.

1258
01:27:02,469 --> 01:27:04,137
Things can't just stop.

1259
01:27:04,262 --> 01:27:05,889
Maybe they should stop.

1260
01:27:06,347 --> 01:27:08,558
Just gonna go on
like nothing happened?

1261
01:27:08,683 --> 01:27:09,559
Snap out of it.

1262
01:27:09,684 --> 01:27:11,561
You can't just leave me
here completely alone

1263
01:27:11,728 --> 01:27:13,104
for eternity with Chuck.

1264
01:27:18,193 --> 01:27:19,068
I know.

1265
01:27:20,320 --> 01:27:21,821
I'm just having a moment.

1266
01:27:23,990 --> 01:27:27,410
There's only two
of us left. And Chuck.

1267
01:27:28,745 --> 01:27:30,121
What are we supposed to do?

1268
01:27:30,747 --> 01:27:33,333
We can just turn one
or two more girls.

1269
01:27:34,334 --> 01:27:36,711
We're not gonna be able
to replace Joan.

1270
01:27:40,799 --> 01:27:42,592
I have my date tonight
with the other hunter,

1271
01:27:42,717 --> 01:27:44,469
and she already shot me
with a silver bullet.

1272
01:27:44,594 --> 01:27:46,554
Shot you?
I thought you killed the hunter.

1273
01:27:46,679 --> 01:27:47,972
That was a different hunter.

1274
01:27:48,223 --> 01:27:49,182
Are you sure?

1275
01:27:49,349 --> 01:27:51,601
How many female hunters
can there be in this town?

1276
01:27:52,227 --> 01:27:56,189
Well, there was at least two
because I just killed one,

1277
01:27:56,648 --> 01:27:58,358
and then the one
I've been dating

1278
01:27:58,483 --> 01:28:00,568
just showed up out of nowhere
and shot me.

1279
01:28:00,693 --> 01:28:03,822
All the chips
were on the table.

1280
01:28:04,531 --> 01:28:08,785
It was time to roll the dice
under one last full moon.

1281
01:28:09,536 --> 01:28:12,747
I only needed one victory
to redeem myself

1282
01:28:12,872 --> 01:28:14,916
from a lifetime of defeats.

1283
01:28:15,041 --> 01:28:17,418
Focus on subduing her
and turning her.

1284
01:28:21,589 --> 01:28:24,175
Just finish my makeup,
and then I'll call her.

1285
01:28:41,651 --> 01:28:44,445
I know you've been right here
in town all along.

1286
01:28:45,321 --> 01:28:47,532
Invite me out
to Club Silver Paradise

1287
01:28:47,657 --> 01:28:50,243
for our date,
like we planned.

1288
01:28:52,245 --> 01:28:53,371
Meet me at the club.

1289
01:28:54,706 --> 01:28:57,458
It's as close to paradise
as you're ever gonna get.

1290
01:28:58,376 --> 01:28:59,836
Thanks for reminding me.

1291
01:29:00,211 --> 01:29:01,296
I'll see you there.

1292
01:29:24,736 --> 01:29:25,820
What's wrong?

1293
01:29:26,195 --> 01:29:27,822
Don't you want to live forever,

1294
01:29:27,947 --> 01:29:29,782
forever, forever, forever?

1295
01:29:31,743 --> 01:29:34,412
The devil was ready
for the violent goodbye.

1296
01:29:35,330 --> 01:29:39,250
No more hide and seek.
No more happy thoughts.

1297
01:29:39,792 --> 01:29:43,004
I had to get close
and make her bleed.

1298
01:29:54,515 --> 01:29:58,186
I've never known a girl
Like you before

1299
01:30:02,231 --> 01:30:05,985
Now, just like in a song
From days of yore

1300
01:30:09,989 --> 01:30:13,493
Here you come a-knocking,
Knocking on my door

1301
01:30:17,288 --> 01:30:21,250
And I've never met a girl
Like you before

1302
01:30:57,829 --> 01:30:59,247
You killed everybody.

1303
01:30:59,664 --> 01:31:00,540
I know.

1304
01:31:01,290 --> 01:31:04,377
This place is dead
and soon you will be too.

1305
01:31:26,357 --> 01:31:28,776
Did I mention how hot you look
with those pistols?

1306
01:32:03,978 --> 01:32:05,688
You know, I just lost
a friend, too.

1307
01:32:06,105 --> 01:32:08,066
We'd been together
for hundreds of years.

1308
01:32:09,108 --> 01:32:10,193
Go to hell.

1309
01:32:10,860 --> 01:32:12,236
I'm already in it.

1310
01:32:28,169 --> 01:32:29,212
Gotta shoot me.

1311
01:32:36,803 --> 01:32:39,680
You're a pretty good shot,
but not good enough.

1312
01:32:40,389 --> 01:32:41,474
Now, it's my turn.

1313
01:33:18,761 --> 01:33:20,346
Eternity doesn't mean much

1314
01:33:20,471 --> 01:33:22,557
if you don't have someone
to share it with.

1315
01:33:23,683 --> 01:33:26,978
Well, what are you waiting for?

1316
01:33:28,354 --> 01:33:29,730
You remind me of Joan.

1317
01:33:32,108 --> 01:33:34,527
I'm not Joan!

1318
01:33:45,663 --> 01:33:48,416
This can go one of two ways, Cora.

1319
01:33:49,876 --> 01:33:53,171
I could just kill you,
and when you die,

1320
01:33:53,671 --> 01:33:57,300
it will be an endless sleep
where there's nothing.

1321
01:33:58,551 --> 01:34:03,139
Or I could turn you,
and we could be friends forever.

1322
01:34:03,264 --> 01:34:04,390
Burn in hell!

1323
01:34:30,750 --> 01:34:32,960
What do you really have
to live for anyway.

1324
01:34:34,295 --> 01:34:36,088
Puppy dogs and ice cream.

1325
01:34:45,556 --> 01:34:46,515
I don't know.

1326
01:34:48,601 --> 01:34:51,020
Do you want to have a drink
and talk about it?

1327
01:34:52,897 --> 01:34:54,690
Guess I'm out of options.

1328
01:34:55,149 --> 01:34:56,067
You're not.

1329
01:34:57,235 --> 01:34:59,445
It's supposed to be
a date anyway.

1330
01:35:25,763 --> 01:35:27,598
You're gonna go blank soon.

1331
01:36:27,825 --> 01:36:29,076
I'm okay, you know?

1332
01:36:29,618 --> 01:36:31,120
That bitch in front
of you is damned.

1333
01:36:31,329 --> 01:36:32,163
I'm fine.

1334
01:36:34,749 --> 01:36:35,958
What does it feel like?

1335
01:36:37,835 --> 01:36:40,379
Well, it definitely feels
really good at first.

1336
01:37:00,024 --> 01:37:01,359
Feels good at first?

1337
01:37:02,443 --> 01:37:03,861
How about after this?

1338
01:37:07,740 --> 01:37:09,909
How's this feel at first?

1339
01:37:11,911 --> 01:37:14,622
Now you're as close
to paradise as you'll ever be.

1340
01:38:40,958 --> 01:38:44,753
Jesus, I thought you'd be
either dead or damned

1341
01:38:44,879 --> 01:38:46,130
by the time we got here.

1342
01:38:46,589 --> 01:38:49,008
War is a game best played
with a grin.

1343
01:38:51,677 --> 01:38:53,304
And you've done a noble job.

1344
01:38:53,929 --> 01:38:55,639
I don't know what noble means.

1345
01:38:55,931 --> 01:38:56,891
You're late.

1346
01:38:59,477 --> 01:39:00,561
Let's sweep the bar.

1347
01:39:01,187 --> 01:39:02,646
There are no survivors.

1348
01:39:05,941 --> 01:39:07,443
Wasn't I so passionate

1349
01:39:07,568 --> 01:39:10,196
about wanting
to kill Elizabeth Bathory

1350
01:39:10,321 --> 01:39:12,072
that I fell in love with her?

1351
01:39:13,699 --> 01:39:18,913
Maybe killing her was the only
happy thing I could think of.

1352
01:39:30,424 --> 01:39:31,300
Oh.

1353
01:39:33,886 --> 01:39:34,803
Oh, shit.

1354
01:39:36,096 --> 01:39:37,389
Did I drink the blood?

1355
01:39:38,766 --> 01:39:40,768
You drank the blood.
You drank the blood.

1356
01:39:40,893 --> 01:39:41,852
You're right.

1357
01:39:42,561 --> 01:39:44,146
I drank the blood.

1358
01:39:50,861 --> 01:39:53,989
I drank the blood,
drank the blood, the blood.

1359
01:39:58,953 --> 01:40:01,413
The memories
would remain shuffled

1360
01:40:01,539 --> 01:40:03,249
like an old deck of cards.

1361
01:40:06,001 --> 01:40:10,839
And the story untold like
a dream that was too sweet.

1362
01:40:12,424 --> 01:40:16,053
The cold, forever night
was finally grinning

1363
01:40:16,178 --> 01:40:19,557
and touching my neck
with its salty breath.

1364
01:40:20,432 --> 01:40:23,143
I became the devil's concubine.

1365
01:40:23,769 --> 01:40:25,229
A servant...

1366
01:40:26,564 --> 01:40:28,357
of the Countess...

1367
01:40:29,024 --> 01:40:32,736
Elizabeth Bathory.

1368
01:40:49,128 --> 01:40:50,296
Hello.

1369
01:40:50,546 --> 01:40:51,714
You look nice.

1370
01:40:55,843 --> 01:40:57,636
I'm hungry and cold.

1371
01:40:58,012 --> 01:41:00,556
I want you to hug me
and take me out to dinner.

